=== PARITY (vs web VehicleHeroWidget.tsx + components/VehicleHero.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (VehicleHeroSource -> VehicleHeroModel):
    useVehicles, useVehicleState, useVehicleLive, useUnits, useSettings. The production app wires
    VehicleHeroSource over those KMP state holders; the view performs NO HTTP. The widget picks the
    vehicle (web `vehicleId ? find ?? [0] : [0]`), reads SI state, and converts at the render boundary.
  Projection (pure, executed-green XCTest):
    • SI->display converters are 1:1 with web unitConversion.ts (METERS_PER_MILE=1609.344, /1000 km,
      /0.3048 ft; mph=*3600/1609.344, km/h=*3.6; °F=*9/5+32). fmtNumber/fmtInt reproduce the global
      precision (2), grouping separators, and the safeNumber NaN/±Inf->0 guard.
    • Gauges: battery(color >50 green / <=50 amber), range(cyan), speed(only when driving||speed>0),
      power(only when charging), inside/outside(temp max 50°C / 122°F) — value/max/unit/color + the
      clamped 0..1 arc + the RadialGauge integer-or-precision value rule.
    • Charging detail: power(kW) / rate(dist/h) / time-to-full(h) + the "Done ~hh:mm" wall-clock.
    • Stat grid: the exact context selection (driving -> speed/power/odometer/ideal; charging ->
      rate/ttf/ideal/odometer; idle -> inside/outside/odometer/ideal) + always (lock/sentry/firmware/
      power) with the web power tint (>0 amber / <0 green / 0 slate) and '—' temp null-guard.
    • Firmware: live.version || live.swUpdateVersion || state.software_version || '—'.
    • Status badge: neutral pill + colored dot from the FSM VEHICLE_STATES badgeDot (online=success,
      driving=#3b82f6, charging=#facc15, parked=#06b6d4, updating=#6366f1, asleep=#a855f7,
      offline=danger), status = state?.state ?? "offline"; unknown -> capitalized neutral fallback.
  Composition -> header (name=display_name||vin + status badge + freshness chip + refresh) · subtitle
    "model trim · vin" · radial-gauge flow · charging panel (charging only) · context stat grid ·
    quick actions (Details/Commands/Live Map/Digital Twin via injected onNavigate) · asleep panel
    ("Vehicle asleep — wake to see live data" + Wake Up) when state is null.
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSSkeleton +
    ContentUnavailableView (compiled against the REAL apps/apple component library in the typechecks
    below). Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (custom SVG gauge -> SwiftUI Circle trim).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty (no vehicle -> ContentUnavailableView) ·
    error (retry affordance) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) ·
    content; PLUS the asleep branch when a vehicle is present but its live state is null. Model phase
    resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell.
